if {metFish} == true:
	if {Inventory.RESUME} == false:
		Manmer: I wonder what i should put in my future cubicle.
		Manmer: Hey, have you found my resume yet? it should be in the tall grass.
		[end_timeline]
	else:
		if {finishedFish} == true:
			Manmer: Thanks again old chap...now I can get back to perparing for my interview.
			Manmer: He starts muttering to himself.
			Manmer: ...Hm... yes, that's a good question. I believe I'm the perfect tuna-can didate for this job because I...
			you: You decide to let him practice in peace.
			[end_timeline]
		else:
			you: Here it is!
			Manmer: Holy m*ckeral.
			He holds up the resume and admires it.
			Manmer: I shouldn’t swear around children.
			Manmer: I thank you from the bottom of my heart!
			Manmer: I’m going to go eat tiramisu to celebrate.
			you: That’s my favorite dessert, too.
			Manmer: Aren’t we are all the same in the grand scheme of things?
			Manmer: Though the future is uncertain, you must always have faith in yourself.
			He looks deep in thought.
			Manmer: When I was little, I had a bad fall on my bicycle.
			Manmer: I broke my leg. It took weeks and weeks to heal.
			Manmer: Alone on the hospital bed, I felt that my leg would be like that forever.
			Manmer: But it healed. Everything requires time, young one.
			Manmer: Thanks for helping a trout out. I’m indebted to you.
			[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"memory":"res://Assets/pictures/manmer_memory.tres"}"]
			you: A memory resurfaces in your mind...
			you: You feel strangely calm. You want to thank him but can’t find the words to.
			set {finishedFish} = true
			[end_timeline]
Manmer: ...
you: He seems sad.
Manmer: My life is DOOMED! i’m letting everyone down..
- Something's fishy here
	Manmer: I'm very sensitive to puns...
	you: I sea
	Manmer: ...
	you: Sorry.
	you: What's wrong?
- What's wrong?
Manmer: The end is near. I can feel the darkness creeping up on me. Tell my family i love them.
Manmer: Our lives are but bits of dust in the infinite universe. each day I feel as if I’m a certain man pushing a stone up a hill.
Manmer: What did you say? "What’s wrong"? Everything is wrong, young one.
- But you’re not a man, you’re a fish
	Manmer: Same thing. We are all the same in the grand scheme of things.
- Sisyphus mention?
	Manmer: SHH...he's going to copyright claim me.
Manmer: I’ve talked too much. if you’ll excuse me, i must go now.
you: Why the hurry?
Manmer: I must continue my search for meaning in this cruel world.
Manmer: ...
Manmer: I must also search for my resume.
- I'll help you!
	Manmer: You are kind.
	Manmer: It might be in the tall grass, could you go search for me?
	you: On it, boss.
- Good luck with that.
	Manmer: You’ll help me, won’t you?
	Manmer: Don’t look at me like that.
	Manmer: Ever since I was a child I wanted to be an investment banker. you’ll help me achieve my dreams, won’t you?
	you: Okay then.
	Manmer: I’m afraid a patch of TALL GRASS is hiding my resume from me. go give it a look, will you?
set {metFish} = true
[signal arg="fishQuest"]
